<title>RUSSIA: Russia to auction 10 trln rbls in bills.</title>
<headline>Russia to auction 10 trln rbls in bills.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Finance Ministry will auction eight trillion roubles in six-month GKO discount Treasury bills (series 22063) and two trillion roubles in a new issue of 18-month OFZ interest-bearing bonds (series 24010) on December 18, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auctions follow:  </p>
<p>Full details of the T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number			    22063</p>
<p>    Issue volume			     8.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date				 Dec 18, 1996</p>
<p>    Tenor					140 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date			    May 7, 1997</p>
<p>Full details of the bond auction:</p>
<p>    Series number			    24010</p>
<p>    Issue volume			     2.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor					546 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date			    June 17, 1998</p>
<p>    First coupon volume		    37.68 pct</p>
<p>    First coupon date			June 18, 1997</p>
<p>    Second coupon date		     Dec 17, 1997</p>
<p>    Third coupon date			June 17, 1998</p>
<p>In money terms the volume of the first coupon is 187,884 roubles.</p>
<p>On December 18 the finance ministry will also repay about 6.12 trillion roubles in maturing three-month T-bills (series 21069).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
